      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When creating guest profiles, consider types of groups that may be more prone to disrupting the quiet atmosphere, such as concert or festival-goers, sports teams on a road trip, or large groups of rowdy college students. You may also want to include profiles for groups of people celebrating special occasions like bachelor/bachelorette parties or anniversaries. Additionally, be mindful of special events like New Year's Eve or large conventions that may attract louder crowds. By identifying these groups, your staff can prepare for potential disruptions and maintain a tranquil environment for other guests. This approach will help you strike a balance between being discreet and proactive.",
